  "details": "There seems to be an internal parameter cap on unsynced bits, yet this isnt documented anywhere. So in my eyes it's a bug.\n\nOne of the avatars I am working on has a lot of local floats for use with a multiplexer system. They have to be part of the expressions parameters, but marked as unsynced to be usable by the menu.\n\nAfter adding a certain amount of non-synced parameters, all parameters in the menu just seem to break. In the VRChat log I get this error:\n\n2024.02.08 06:46:24 Error      -  [Behaviour] Unable to initialize stage parameters, defined parameters use more memory then allowed.\n\nMy avatar is using 220 bits of synced data, and then around 30 local floats for the multiplexer system and some other things.\n\nIt specifically seems to break OSC sync when this happens.",
